\section{Research Interests}
My research focuses on applying AI to \textbf{drug discovery}, with the goal of modeling how small molecules act in biological systems.
I began with \textbf{compound--cell response prediction}, ranking the gene expression changes that drug perturbations induce in cells~[\ref{pub:badger}].
I then moved to the molecule level with \textbf{activity cliff prediction}, capturing how subtle structural differences between molecules lead to large changes in activity~[\ref{pub:graphcliff}],
and most recently to \textbf{drug metabolism}, predicting cytochrome P450 sites of metabolism across isoforms~[\ref{pub:attnsom}].

\smallskip
Beyond this main line, I have worked on \textbf{retrosynthesis planning}~[\ref{pub:retro}] and \textbf{compound--protein interaction prediction}~[\ref{pub:perceivercpi}],
as well as \textbf{biomedical natural language processing}, including LLM-based biomedical question answering and radiology report summarization~[\ref{pub:bioasq}, \ref{pub:radsum}].

